  "description": "From TASK-7.13 review: the approved hand order (equity vs one random hand) ranks Q2o/J2o/K2o above suited connectors (76s/65s/87s), the opposite of how loose limit players choose hands; and scaling every raising line by PFR widens re-raise ranges a lot (a 22/18 player's UTG four-bet range goes 2.56% \u2192 18% at 100 hands). Options: keep; switch to a playability-weighted order (e.g. equity vs a typical calling range, or an authored order); scale re-raise lines by a 3-bet stat instead of PFR.",
